conde session vivante (e09).\n=====\nbugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-26T142500\n    date: \"2026-09-26\"\n    title: \"Pausing a stopped change erases its stop, and a resume can no longer lift it\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: domain\n    what_happened: >\n      A change blocked on a stop a resume lifts (a stalled specification, an execution error) accepted\n      `/495 pause`. On resume it came back `blocked` with no stop reason, no detail and no longer\n      retryable: a second resume lifted nothing, the names of the lost answers were gone, and cancel\n      was the only way out left.\n    what_expected: >\n      A stopped change keeps its stop, its detail and its ways out whatever the operator does before\n      lifting it.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Take a change to the stop before G0 of a specification that no longer progresses.\"\n      - \"Run `/495 pause`, then `/495 resume` twice.\"\n      - \"The change stays `blocked` with `stop_reason` null and `stop_retryable` false, and `advance` writes nothing.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      `changePause` (`src/domain/change/decide.ts`) accepted any active change, blocked ones included.\n      It saved only the status in the resume point, and its `status.changed` event cleared the stop\n      reason, detail and retryability. `changeResume` restored `blocked` without them, and\n      `harness.resume` lifts a block only when its reason is `execution_error` or it is retryable. The\n      same code is on main for every stop a resume lifts; a stalled specification relies on that\n      resume for its recourse.\n    evidence: >\n      test/v0/change-rules.test.ts, \"refuses to pause a blocked change, which keeps its stop, its detail\n      and its retryability\", and test/v2/specification-reopening.test.ts, \"refuses to pause a stopped\n      change, whose stop a resume still lifts into a rewriting (6a)\": red at 0d67f46 (2 failures out\n      of 59, the pause accepted), green at 6d5a3e3, both in a detached worktree. Preflight green under\n      Node 26.9.0, 486 tests.\n    reopened: >\n      The guard `6d5a3e3` added to `changePause` left a second way in: a change blocked while an\n      intervention still ran. A `DomainError` thrown between `intervention.start` and\n      `intervention.finish` (a missing adopted artifact, a failed store write, a worker that does not\n      start) blocked the change and left the intervention `running`. `harness.pause` finishes a running\n      intervention before it commits `change.pause`, and `intervention.finished` sets the status to\n      `ready`: the guard saw a ready change, accepted the pause, and the stop was erased. The kernel now\n      ends the running intervention in `block`, in the same decision as the stop, so a blocked change\n      never has one: red at 287123c (3 failures out of 93), green at d6b0bd5, both in a detached\n      worktree. Preflight green under Node 26.9.0, 490 tests.\n    risk_level: medium\n    follow_ups: \"none\"\n    status: fixed\n    fixed_in: d6b0bd5\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-26T145000\n    date: \"2026-09-26\"\n    title: \"A resume lifts a stop no resume may lift when the step failed while its intervention ran\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: application\n    what_happened: >\n      A change blocked on a missing capability, an invalid configuration or a policy refusal, by a step\n      that failed while its intervention ran, came back `ready` on `/495 resume`. No `change.unblock`\n      was recorded, so the lift was neither judged by the kernel nor attributed to the human who\n      resumed.\n    what_expected: >\n      A resume lifts only an execution error or a stop the kernel declared retryable, under the actor\n      who resumed; any other stop stays in place.\n=====\ne01s05\ne03s01\ne03s02\ne23-deux-fournisseurs.md\ne23s05-budgets-remesures.md\ne23s06-strate-observee.md\ne25s04-modele-choisi-admis.md\nreprise-de-verification-et-revocation\nspecs/verificatio